<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>RESULTS
OF OPERATIONS FOR THE THREE MONTH PERIOD ENDED SEPTEMBER 30, 2024</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">The
following is an analysis of the Company&rsquo;s operating results for the three month period ended September 30, 2024, and includes a
comparison against the three month period ended September 30, 2023.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Operations:</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Revenues
</B>for the three month period ended September 30, 2024, were $5,862,575 compared to $1,842,390 for the three month period ended September
30, 2023. This increase period over period of $4,020,186 (positive 218% of revenues) is mainly due to a $4,523,599 increase in the sale
of rugged devices, (a 426% period over period increase due to the maturation of the SD7 product line) and a decrease by a $501,390 (64%
decrease) in the sale of boosters for the period.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"></P>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 56; Value: 2 -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><P STYLE="font: normal 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->56<!-- Field: /Sequence --></P></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Gross
Margin </B>for the three month period ended September 30, 2024, was $1,703,033
(29.0% of sales) compared to $490,097 (26.6% of sales) for the three month period ended September 30, 2023. a positive variance in gross
margin dollars of $1,212,936 (2.4% increase in gross margin percentage). This relates to the increase in sales by 426% in rugged devices
in North America at higher margins, offset by both the sale in the EMEA of discontinued merchandise resulting at reduced margins as well
aa due to the 64% decrease in cellular boosters in the quarter.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Amortization
and depreciation costs </B>for the three month period ended September 30, 2024, were $424,393 compared to $453,500 for the three month
period ended September 30, 2023, a positive variance of $29,107 related to decrease in amortization of R&amp;D amortization in North
America in 2023, that was fully amortized by 2024 in the amount of $35,302 and partially offset by the $6,195 increase in the amortization
of fixed assets in the period</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Development
expenses</B> for the three month period ended September 30, 2024, were $294,753 compared to $87,652 for the three month period ended
September 30, 2023, This negative variance of $207,101 is due to the discontinued capitalization of costs related to the SD7+ that did
not meet the criteria for capitalization in 2024 and 2023.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Selling
and marketing </B>costs for the three month period ended September 30, 2024, were $1,367,546 compared to $743,760 for the three month
period ended September 30, 2023.This negative variance of $623,786 is due mainly to the increase in U.S. sales team headcount and commission
structure resulting in a negative variance of $527,300, an increase in travel expense of $45,221 due to more focused travel in the period
and an increase in promotional costs of $51,265.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Equity
promotion and marketing </B>costs for the three month period ended September 30, 2024, were $2,190,162 compared to $540,000 for the three
month period ended September 30, 2023.This negative variance of $1,650,162 is due mainly to the increase in equity promotion expenses
to increase company awareness in the investor community.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Inventory
income from water damage </B>for the three months ended September 30, 2024, was $NIL compared to
income of $405,364 for the three months ended September 30, 2023, respectively. This negative variance relates to previously written off
inventory from the December 2022 flood that was determined to be salvageable and reinstated into income for the quarter ended September
2023.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>General
and administrative </B>costs for the three month period ended September 30, 2024, was $1,166,461 compared to $1,458,284 for the three
month period ended September 30, 2023. This positive variance of $291,823 (-20%) relates mainly to the decrease in professional services
costs of $210,641 related to the decrease in fees for the annual PCAOB audit preparation costs, a decrease in office and general expenses
of $80,228 related to the decrease in D&amp;O insurance costs, , decrease in regulatory and filing fees of $10,714, decrease in shareholder
relations of $44,960, the decrease of $5,691 in travel costs, and the decrease of $19,010 in salaries expense offset by an increase in
consulting and directors fees of $79,421.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Bad
debts </B>for the three month period ended September 30, 2024, were $8,132 compared to $16,152 for the three month period ended September
30, 2023, a positive variance of $8,380.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Insurance
proceeds from the water damage</B> of $NIL in the three month period ended September 30, 2024 and $380,077
was received during the three month period ended September 30, 2023. This amount from 2023 was included as income in the 2023 period received
as required by IFRS.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Share-based
</B>compensation costs for the three month period ended September 30, 2024, were $54,682 compared to $202,072 for the three month period
ended September 30, 2023, a positive variance of $147,390. The decrease in share-based compensation relates to the valuation of stock
options vested during the period due to the issuance in 2022 of 243 Restricted share units and 119 stock options to employees, management
and directors in 2022 which are amortized over three years resulting in a lower amount closer to complete vesting.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Finance
expenses </B>for the three month period ended September 30, 2024 were $527,962 compared
to $33,684 for the three month period ended September 30, 2023, a negative variance of $494,278. This variance consists of the increase
in finance fees and related interest expenses on the factoring facility of $214,494, the interest on a bank loan of $25,379, increase
in bank charges of $20,968 and the increase in the interest on the sale of future receipts of $234,219, offset by a decrease in IFRS16
finance costs and other bank charges of $782.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"></P>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 57; Value: 2 -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><P STYLE="font: normal 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->57<!-- Field: /Sequence --></P></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Foreign
exchange loss (gain) </B>for the three month period ended September 30, 2024, were negative
$26,592 compared to negative $109,895 for the three month period ended September 30, 2023, a negative variance of $83,303. This variance
resulted from foreign currency fluctuations in the period.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Change
in fair value of the preferred share liability </B>for the three month period ended September 30, 2024 was a gain of $386,022 compared
to $NIL for the three month period ended September 30, 2023, a positive variance of $386,022. This variance relates to the change in
fair value that is recorded as profit in loss on the financial liability instrument.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Gain
on settlement of derivative </B>for the three month period ended September 30, 2024 was a gain of $3,723,827 compared to $NIL for the
three month period ended September 30, 2023, a positive variance of $3,723,827. This variance relates to the non-cash income earned on
the difference in fair value on the exchange of certain outstanding warrants in exchange for 293 Class &ldquo;C&rdquo; preferred shares
of the Company in this three month.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Change
in fair value of the warrant liability </B>for the three month period ended September 30, 2024 was a loss of $3,900 compared to a gain
of $294,858 for the three month period ended September 30, 2023, a negative variance of $298,758. This variance relates to the change
in fair value that is recorded as profit in loss on the financial liability derivatives.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Transaction
costs </B>for the three month period ended September 30, 2024 was $427,812 compared to $NIL for the three month period ended September
30, 2023. This variance relates to the transaction costs incurred due to multiple capital raises where the portion of these raises that
relate to a financial instrument are treated as a liability and not equity, and so the related costs incurred are expenses in the period
as transaction costs and not as share issuance costs.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Net
loss and Comprehensive loss for the period</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">The Company experienced a net loss for the three month period ended
September 30, 2024 of $626,329 compared to a net loss of $1,855,173 for the three month period ended September 30, 2023, a positive variance
of $1,228,844. This positive variance was mainly due to the increase in gross margin dollars of $1,212,936, a decrease in amortization
of $29,107, a decrease in bad debt expense by $8,380, a decrease in G&amp;A expenses of $291,823, a decrease in share-based payments of
$147,390, an increase in gain on settlement of derivative of $3,723,827, and an increase in the fair value gain on financial derivatives
of $87,264, offset by an increase in development expense of $207,101, an increase in selling expenses of $623,786, an increase in equity
marketing and promotion of $1,650,162, decrease in inventory income from water damage of $405,364, a decrease in insurance proceeds from
water damage of $380,077, an increase in finance expenses of $494,278, increase in transaction costs of $427,812, decrease in foreign
exchange gain of $83,303.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Adjusted
EBITDA </B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">For
the three month period ended September 30, 2024, the adjusted EBITDA was negative 3,324,021 compared to $1,570,670 for the three month
period ended September 30, 2023, a negative variance of $1,753,351. Adjusted EBITDA is defined as the net operating loss excluding depreciation
and amortization, and share-based compensation expense. It is a non-IFRS calculation that should be compared to our audited financial
information included elsewhere in this Annual Report</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>RESULTS
OF OPERATIONS FOR THE NINE MONTH PERIOD ENDED SEPTEMBER 30, 2024</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">The
following is an analysis of the Company&rsquo;s operating results for the nine month period ended September 30, 2024, and includes a
comparison against the nine month period ended September 30, 2023.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Operations:</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Revenues
</B>for the nine month period ended September 30, 2024, were $10,111,422 compared to $6,355,744 for the nine month period ended September
30, 2023. This increase period over period of $3,755,678 (positive 59% of revenues) is mainly due to a 100% increase in the sale of rugged
devices (maturation of the SD7 product line) by $4,556,655 and a decrease by a $903,000 (50.0% decrease) in the sale of boosters for
the period.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"></P>

