<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Gross
Margin</B> for the nine month period ended September 30, 2024, was $2,763,264 (27.3% of sales) compared to $1,791,104 (28.2% of sales)
for the nine month period ended September 30, 2023. a positive variance in gross margin by $972,160 (54.3% increase in gross margin dollars
and a 0.9% decrease in gross margin percentage). This large increase in gross margin dollars is due to the 55% increase in sales in the
USA market for the year to date over prior year to date.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Amortization
and depreciation costs </B>for the nine month period ended September 30, 2024, were $1,262,180 compared to $1,308,639 for the nine month
period ended September 30, 2023, a positive variance of $46,4592 related to the decrease in amortization of the IFRS16 assets.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Development
expenses</B> for the nine month period ended September 30, 2024, were $329,753 compared to $173,102 for the nine month period ended September
30, 2023, This negative variance of $156, is 651 is due to the discontinued capitalization of costs related to the SD7+ that did not
meet the criteria for capitalization in 2024 and 2023.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Selling
and marketing </B>costs for the nine month period ended September 30, 2024, were $3,469,952 compared to $2,734,928 for the nine month
period ended September 30, 2023.This negative variance of $735,024 is due mainly to the increase in U.S. sales team headcount and commission
structure resulting in a negative variance of $800,300 and an increase in travel expense of $21,762 due to more focused travel in the
period, offset by a decrease in promotional marketing of $88,663.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Equity
promotion and marketing </B>costs for the nine month period ended September 30, 2024, were $4,340,162 compared to $1,131,20 for the nine
month period ended September 30, 2023. This negative variance of $3,208,962 is due mainly to the increase in equity promotion expenses
to increase company awareness in the investor community.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Inventory
income from water damage </B>for the nine months ended September 30, 2024, was $NIL compared to $405,364 for the nine months ended September
30, 2023, respectively. This negative variance relates to previously written off inventory from the December 2022 flood that was determined
to be salvageable and reinstated into income for the quarter ended September 2023.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>General
and administrative </B>costs for the nine month period ended September 30, 2024, was $3,238,314 compared to $4,012,896 for the nine month
period ended September 30, 2023. This positive variance of $774,582 (19%) relates mainly to the decrease in professional services costs
of $649,641 related to the decrease in fees for the annual PCAOB audit preparation costs, a decrease in office and general expenses of
$206,124 related to the decrease in D&amp;O insurance costs, decrease in regulatory and filing fees of $23,714, decrease in shareholder
relations of $64,823, and a decrease of $15,010 in salaries expense offset by an increase of $23,309 in travel costs, and an increase
in consulting and directors fees of $161,421.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Bad
debts </B>for the nine month period ended September 30, 2024, were $26,990 compared to $26,660 for the nine month period ended September
30, 2023, a negative variance of $330.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Insurance
proceeds from the water damage</B> of $NIL in the nine month period ended September 30, 2024 and $380,077 was received during the three
month period ended September 30, 2023. This amount from 2023 was included as income in the period received as required by IFRS.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Share-based
</B>compensation costs for the nine month period ended September 30, 2024, were $255,568 compared to $773,605 for the nine month period
ended September 30, 2023, a positive variance of $518,037. The decrease in share-based compensation relates to the valuation of stock
options vested during the period due to the issuance in 2022 of 243 Restricted share units and 119 stock options to employees, management
and directors in 2022 which are amortized over three years resulting in a lower amount closer to complete vesting.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Finance
expenses</B> for the nine month period ended September 30, 2024 were $2,250,001
compared to $109,033 for the nine month period ended September 30, 2023, a negative variance of $2,140,968. This variance consists of
the increase in finance fees and related interest expenses on the factoring facility of $258,110, the increase in finance expenses related
to the sale of future receivables in the amount of $1,802,673, the interest on a bank loan of $81,974 plus a decrease in IFRS16 finance
costs and other bank charges of $1,789.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"></P>

